<Base title="About" description="About me and my work.">
  <h1>About</h1>
  <p>
    I'm Dimitris Pantazis, a software developer from Greece. My non-greek friends and coworkers call me <span class="font-bold">Dimi</span>.
  </p>
  <p>
    I've started my professional journey in the world of software development in 2018. My first touch with code though was in 2008 when i was 14 years old and i was playing DOTA (Defense of the Ancients) in Warcraft 3.
    Back then, various bots were created by the community and i was one of those people for whom the bots weren't doing exactly what i wanted them to... So i had to see their code and understand how they worked!
  </p>
  <p>
    Nowadays, I'm working as a Senior Software Engineer at <a href="https://stellarworks.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">StellarWP</a>, where i help maintain and
    build new features for <a href="https://theeventscalendar.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Events Calendar</a> products and various other StellarWP products.
  </p>
  <p>
    I also do work on other projects through my agency <a href="https://pantadev.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Panta Dev</a>! If you're interested in working with me, feel free to <a href="mailto:dimi@pantadev.com">reach out</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    My expertise lies in helping businesses of any size, from startups to enterprise, with their needs. That doesn't has to be a WordPress project necessarily, since
    I am experienced in working with a variety of technologies and frameworks! Laravel, Symfony, React, Next, Vue, Express, Nest and more ! You name it and i've probably worked with it!
  </p>
  <p>
    I have worked extensively with WordPress, both as a developer and as a consultant. I have worked with a variety of plugins and themes, and have a deep understanding of the WordPress ecosystem.
    Some of my expertise related to WordPress projects includes: WooCommerce, WooCommerce Subscriptions, WooCommerce Memberships, The Events Calendar and Event Tickets, Learndash and more!
  </p>
  <p>
    I am also a big advocate of well tested and documented code. I believe that code should be easy to understand, easy to maintain and safe to update! Without surprises!
  </p>
</Base>